dby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T03:38:05-07:00","id":1235853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1235841#post1235841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, ghosts have \u201cInfluence: (My) Anchor\u201d after all?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes: at least one dot is usually Influence (Anchors).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T03:46:44-07:00","id":1235856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1235853#post1235853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes: at least one dot is usually Influence (Anchors).</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it about the specific thing they\u2019re Anchored to, Anchor-ness in general, or their own Anchor-ness?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T06:04:16-07:00","id":1235880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e#post1235817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that we gave Geist's rules for ghost creation, we can start making some of our own. Post your's here!</div> </div> </div> </div>Where in Kickstarter Preview are Ghosts rules? In Chapter 4? Are not those typical rules for Ephemeral Entites, like in every other CoD 2E rulebook? Absent - playable ghosts - were not uncovered yet, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T06:27:54-07:00","id":1235886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1235841#post1235841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, ghosts have \u201cInfluence: (My) Anchor\u201d after all?</div> </div> </div> </div>It turns out that Sanctity of Influences is also a thing, and the emphasis on Anchors as Things That Were Important To The Ghost And/Or Their Death, combined with the ability to use more tenuous personal connections to subjects from their lives to apply the Condition to those things through magic (and, of course, the body or gravesite being a common Anchor), makes the notion of Influence: Things That Fall Within The Ghost's Sphere Of Influence not quite as redundant as initially surmised.<br /> <br /> The fact that ghosts are inherently temporary and have greater access to a universal Open Condition makes the notion that they could theoretically run out of viable Anchors less of an issue, and Rank working the way it does means ghosts technically having Influence: My Own Life doesn't break much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-17-2018, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T06:50:58-07:00","id":1235893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1235856#post1235856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it about the specific thing they\u2019re Anchored to, Anchor-ness in general, or their own Anchor-ness?</div> </div> </div> </div>Far as I can Remember Right now, it is the specific place, thing or person.<br /> So rather than *Anchor 2, as I wrote, I should have written Crossroad 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T06:56:05-07:00","id":1235898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1235886#post1235886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It turns out that Sanctity of Influences is also a thing, and the emphasis on Anchors as Things That Were Important To The Ghost And/Or Their Death, combined with the ability to use more tenuous personal connections to subjects from their lives to apply the Condition to those things through magic (and, of course, the body or gravesite being a common Anchor), makes the notion of Influence: Things That Fall Within The Ghost's Sphere Of Influence not quite as redundant as initially surmised.<br /> <br /> The fact that ghosts are inherently temporary and have greater access to a universal Open Condition makes the notion that they could theoretically run out of viable Anchors less of an issue, and Rank working the way it does means ghosts technically having Influence: My Own Life doesn't break much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so Anchors are broader and more flexible than what I thought. Cool. <br /> <br /> <br /> * groundless speculation time<br /> A while ago I floated around the possibility of playable ghosts being playable by virtue of being more connected to their human identities, represented by having Influence over their Anchors instead of things like Sadness or Fire, which I expected would also make player-controlled Influence more manageable. Now, Anchors really do seem to be intimately connected to a ghost\u2019s \u201cpast\u201d life, or at least their memories of it. And the Absent, the playable ghosts, have been mentioned to be able to do something with memories. Hmm...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T07:02:39-07:00","id":1235902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1235893#post1235893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Far as I can Remember Right now, it is the specific place, thing or person.<br /> So rather than *Anchor 2, as I wrote, I should have written Crossroad 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, this kinda clashes with what Satchel just wrote, with Anchor as Influence essentially being \u201cThings Important To Me,\u201d doesn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> ... Or I\u2019m suffering dice penalties to Reading rolls due to exhaustion, and failed a roll somewhere. Quite likely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T07:04:46-07:00","id":1235903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1235898#post1235898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so Anchors are broader and more flexible than what I thought. Cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more flexible in aggregate, but the practical reality is still typically &quot;these one to three specific things, folded under an umbrella category of 'Anchors.'&quot;<br /> <br /> Numina and Manifestations and Plasm fill the gap vis-a-vis ghostly supernatural phenomena; the mechanics paint a pretty clear picture of the Underworld as not really where ghosts are <i>supposed</i> to go, and the nature of Anchors seems to be part of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T07:22:51-07:00","id":1235911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1235903#post1235903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more flexible in aggregate, but the practical reality is still typically &amp;quot;these one to three specific things, folded under an umbrella category of 'Anchors.'&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly that\u2019s <i>still</i> broader than what I used to think, so I\u2019m happy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the mechanics paint a pretty clear picture of the Underworld as not really where ghosts are <i>supposed</i> to go, and the nature of Anchors seems to be part of that. </div> </div> </div>To the starry fields of A\u2019aru, then!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T07:59:10-07:00","id":1235923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1235818#post1235818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not an entry, but a request from someone who doesn\u2019t have access to the Kickstarter previews; what would a Sadako expy look like under the 2e rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess her Anchor would be the cursed videotape, including any copies of it. She'd have both the Anchor Jump and Hallucinate Numina, and the Fetter and Materialize Manifestations. She'd have a somewhat complicated Ban to the tune of &quot;Can only Materialize to kill someone and can only kill someone seven days after they've watched the cursed tape if they have not made a copy and shown someone else.&quot; I guess that once you watch the tape, she starts using Influences to make sure that you're Open to her for when the time comes (also explaining the weird dreams and uncanny phenomena that follow the watcher).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T08:11:44-07:00","id":1235927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1235923#post1235923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess her Anchor would be the cursed videotape, including any copies of it. She'd have both the Anchor Jump and Hallucinate Numina, and the Fetter and Materialize Manifestations. She'd have a somewhat complicated Ban to the tune of &quot;Can only Materialize to kill someone and can only kill someone seven days after they've watched the cursed tape if they have not made a copy and shown someone else.&quot; I guess that once you watch the tape, she starts using Influences to make sure that you're Open to her for when the time comes (also explaining the weird dreams and uncanny phenomena that follow the watcher).</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. Though now that I think of it, Sadako\u2019s powers are weird even for the CofD. I don\u2019t remember clearly if it was her, but I swear in one movie she managed to rebirth herself. As in, physically being born from a pregnant woman. *shudders","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T08:28:08-07:00","id":1235931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1235927#post1235927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nice. Though now that I think of it, Sadako\u2019s powers are weird even for the CofD. I don\u2019t remember clearly if it was her, but I swear in one movie she managed to rebirth herself. As in, physically being born from a pregnant woman. *shudders</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is true. And book-Sadako does some even weirder stuff, what with replicating herself as a virus. I think in a CofD scenario, she'd be well on her way to Geisthood, if not something even stranger.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-17T08:31:09-07:00","id":1235933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1235880#post1235880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where in Kickstarter Preview are Ghosts rules? In Chapter 4? Are not those typical rules for Ephemeral Entites, like in every other CoD 2E rulebook? Absent - playable ghosts - were not uncovered yet, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are, but there are also new Numina specific to ghosts and different types of Ghosts that have not been featured before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-20T21:04:58-07:00","id":1237395,"title":"","content":"(Reading Ghosts rules in depth) So Ghosts have Skills and Merits on them? Will need to hack more a Ghosts Sheet for CoD gamelines with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24\" data-vbnamecard=\"24\">Mr Gone</a>... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-21-2018, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T09:38:58-07:00","id":1237774,"title":"","content":"Now that I am properly updated with the Manuscript, I have revised a few of my ghosts! <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Drowned Woman</b></span><br /> She remembers drowning. It happened so long ago that she has forgotten her name or exactly how she ended up on that ship. But she remembers the storm; months too early in the season and with rain like blades and waves like the fists of an angry god. She remembers the crack of the vessel being torn in half and the cold of the water filling her lungs. She haunted that stretch of coast for decades \u2013tied to a locket given to her by someone she loved (perhaps a husband or fianc\u00e9). But eventually that was worn away by time and tide as well. In life she was a willful woman, and she has continued on in the underworld, becoming a traveler and guide well versed in the many rivers, lakes, and seas that exist within the underworlds winding caverns.<br /> The Drowned Woman appears as a slender woman with bright red hair that stands out against her deathly pale skin and has eyes the color of seawater. Her age is indeterminate, seeming middle aged or youthful by turns. She is dressed in a simple white gown and is perpetually drenched in water as if she just emerged from the waves. She has a lovely voice and sings sea shanties with gusto and skill.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Geist]<br /> <b>Power</b> 8 <b>Finesse</b> 8, <b>Resistance</b> 6, <b>Willpower</b> 10, <b>Essence</b> 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 11, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 14, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Kind, <b>Vice</b> Headstrong<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To help those that travel by waterway<br /> <b>Remembrance:</b> Expression<br /> <b>Innate Key:</b> Key of Deep Waters<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot board a vessel without offering payment to the Captain <b>Bane:</b> Tokens of Romantic Affection<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Discorporate, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Banshee Wail*, Emotional Aura (Loss), Pathfinder, Seek, Telekinesis<br /> <b><i>Numina \u2013 Banshee Wail:</i></b> The entity creates an earsplitting scream that deafens anyone nearby. Anyone within 20 yards of the entity must succeed on a Resolve + Stamina roll \u2013 the number of successes gained or suffer the Stunned and Deafened Tilt. The Numen costs one Essence to activate.</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Lost Ronin</span></b><br /> The Lost Ronin lived during the waning days of Tokugawa era Japan, and was a Ronin Samurai known for his love of drinking and gambling, and for his entitled attitude towards the peasantry (or anyone else he considered beneath him). After a particularly ugly incident at a gambling hall, he was ambushed by a group of assailants while too drunk to defend himself, as was murdered. His corpse was buried deep in a field and the murderers never spoke of the incident again. His angry spirit lingers on, enraged that he was slain by peasants while drunk, and denied a death befitting a Samurai. Quenching his thirst in the Rivers of Meido have made the Ronin strong, and he longs for re-entry to the world of the living, for only there can he earn a true, worthy, death.<br /> The Lost Ronin has forgotten many details about his mortal life and his appearance has taken on an indistinct quality \u2013 a straw hat that obscures his face and a tattered dark blue kimono are the most striking elements, all other details are a water-color blur.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Geist]<br /> <b>Power</b> 8 <b>Finesse</b> 8,<b> Resistance</b> 8, <b>Willpower</b> 10, <b>Essence</b> 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 13, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Proud, <b>Vice</b> Entitled<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> to be put to rest in a manner befitting a samurai<br /> <b>Remembrance:</b> Weaponry<br /> <b>Innate Key:</b> Key of Blood<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot refuse a challenge to a Duel <b>Bane:</b> A katana blade wielded by a Samurai (or member of a similar warrior elite)<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Avernian Gateway, Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Phantom Arsenal (Sword)*, Regenerate, Seek, Speed, Telekinesis<br /> <i><b>Numina \u2013 Phantom Arsenal:</b></i> The entity spends 1 Essence point to manifest blades, claws, fangs, hooks or other appropriate weaponry. The modification acts as a +1L weapon. By spending an additional point of essence, this weapon gains the \u201c9-Again\u201d quality.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 07-26-2018, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T01:30:20-07:00","id":1238530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e#post1235817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that we gave Geist's rules for ghost creation, we can start making some of our own. Post your's here!</div> </div> </div> </div>This initially threw me off, as I at first thought you were talking about the Absent. And we don't yet have <i>playable</i> ghost creation. Soon, though; very soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T06:29:01-07:00","id":1238571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1238530#post1238530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This initially threw me off, as I at first thought you were talking about the Absent. And we don't yet have <i>playable</i> ghost creation. Soon, though; very soon.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair - we<i> already</i> got XP costs for <b>all</b> ghosts characters. I easily could implement those also for Spirits in <b>Werewolf </b>and Dreamborn in <b>Beast</b> PCs - which I gladly do! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T09:06:53-07:00","id":1238596,"title":"","content":"Which is great for <i>advancing</i> ghost characters; but not necessarily for <i>playing</i> them.<br /> <br /> My guess is that there are going to be a few differences between the Absent and other ghosts, differences that are designed to make ghosts more playable. Things like a Memory stat instead of Integrity; like maybe putting Virtue and Vice back in their usual orientation, or at least explaining what it means to be able to access your Virtue so easily while having to work at benefitting from your Vice; like maybe giving you more access to your former Skills and Merits (possibly through your Memory); possibly addressing how Numina work for playable characters when they were originally devised with Storyteller characters in mind; and giving you an explanation for <i>why</i> the Absent are different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T09:43:13-07:00","id":1238607,"title":"","content":"All things that would make playable ghosts more enjoyable (and thus better reason to want to play ghosts) but it's primarily Essence management that need to be expanded for playable ghost to become actually playable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T10:33:55-07:00","id":1238620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1238596#post1238596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is great for <i>advancing</i>or at least explaining what it means to be able to access your Virtue so easily while having to work at benefitting from your Vice;</div> </div> </div> </div>I may have misread or misunderstood something, but my impression of the Vice/Virtue flip is simply the way it earns WP, in other words it's easier to get all your WP back by indulging in the easy thing that's your Vice than it is to get any WP back from engaging your Virtue. Which makes sense to me considering the tortured state of ghosts, and the fact that they're trying to cling to their identity more than they're concerned with growing toward being a better person like the living are supposed to be doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T11:53:21-07:00","id":1238643,"title":"","content":"My partner reminded me myths about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dullahan\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Dullahan</b></a> - Headless Horseman in Irish folklore. Cool would be to have it for the <b>Geist</b> games. I suppose in <b>GtSE</b> 2E Dullahan would work as Geist, maybe Reaper ( they can be both at the same time? ) that are hunting mortals ( and dead sometimes ). Anyone for ballparking it's stats?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T19:44:41-07:00","id":1239159,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Dullahan</b><br /> <br /> I have the done Dullahan as a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1071008#post1071008\">Horror</a> and a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1164036-a-hodgepodge-of-hobs-2nd-ed?p=1164213#post1164213\">Hobgoblin</a>, so here is the Reaper version. I also added another Geist just for fun. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Dullahan</span></b><br /> The Reaper known as \u201cThe Dullahan\u201d is a nightmarish vision of a headless horseman clad in black riding leathers and wrapped in a dark cloak. A relentless hunter, once its prey is chosen, few things can deter it. Not satisfied with just the dead, it is known to strike at the living fated to die, dragging their their freshly manifested ghosts back to the Underworld. Those wearing the Black Mantle of the Dullahan appear as a tall man (or woman) with lean, athletic frames, and carry their severed heads with them or keep them nearby. The Dullahan is always accompanied by a spectral mount or vehicle of some sort, typically a midnight black stallion, but occasionally they appear with horse drawn coach, motorcycle or car. As The Dullahan, the Reaper carries a sword and a whip. Victims are ensnared by the whip and engulf into the folds of the Black Mantle. Where the captured ghosts are taken is a mystery to even other Reapers, but none are ever seen again. The current Dullahan is a ghost named Christoph, who in life was a notoriously blood thirsty Hessian mercenary. These days he rarely sheds his Deathmask and spends nearly every moment as The Dullahan.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2/4 [Reaper]<br /> <b>Power</b> 7/12 <b>Finesse</b> 3/9, <b>Resistance</b> 4/12, <b>Willpower</b> 7/10, <b>Essence</b> 15/25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9/17, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 7/21, <b>Defense</b> 3/9, <b>Speed</b> 15/26<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Determined, <b>Vice</b> Ominous<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To herald impending death<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Anchor (Skull) 2, <i>Doom 2</i><br /> <b>Ban (Christoph):</b> Cannot approach anyone carrying his mortal remain <b>Bane (Christoph)</b>: Gold<br /> <b>Ban (Dullahan):</b> Cannot enter a House of Worship <b>Bane (Dullahan):</b> Religious icons made of Gold<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> <i>Avernian Gate</i>, Discorporate, Image, <i>Materialize</i>, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, <i>Descend</i>, <i>Engulf</i>, Pathfinder, Phantom Arsenal**, <i>Regeneration</i>,<i> Snare**</i>, <i>Speed</i>, Telekinesis<br /> <br /> <b>Numina- Snare:</b> As per the Dread Power (CofD, pg. 147)<br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Phantom Arsenal:</b> The entity spends 1 Essence point to manifest blades, claws, fangs, hooks or other appropriate weaponry. The modification acts as a +1L weapon. By spending an additional point of essence, this weapon gains the \u201c9-Again\u201d quality.</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Bleak Cardinal</b></span><br /> The Geist named the Bleak Cardinal can recall only fragments of its mortal life. Once, it was a man of the cloth and respected figure within his community. But he had long ago lost his faith in both man and God and every confession taken only increased his despair. Cast into Purgatory upon his death, he sought redemption, eventually enduring a second baptism in the waters of the Styx. The Bleak Cardinal now seeks redemption and salvation, hoping to help lost souls move beyond purgatory and earn their final rest.<br /> The Bleak Cardinal appears as a bearded, skeletal corpse, dressed in red vestments of a catholic Cardinal His eyes blaze with a bright light and he speak in a quite, whispering voice with an educated eloquent manner of speaking.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Geist]<br /> <b>Power</b> 9 <b>Finesse</b> 8, <b>Resistance</b> 7, <b>Willpower</b> 10, <b>Essence</b> 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 12, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 15, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 22<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Compassion, <b>Vice</b> Doubt<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To Regain his Faith<br /> <b>Remembrance:</b> Persuasion<br /> <b>Innate Key:</b> Key of Cold Wind<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot harm members of the Clergy <b>Bane:</b> Communion Wine<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Bargain, Discorporate., Image, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast, Drain, Emotional Aura, Rapture, Sign, Telekinesis</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 07-26-2018, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T20:02:45-07:00","id":1239164,"title":"","content":"Great stuff, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a>, as always! Cannot wait to use your's Dullahan on players! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And Black Cardinal makes so much cool Geist to use! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T14:24:53-07:00","id":1239437,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"https://pre00.deviantart.net/1480/th/pre/i/2012/302/2/3/celty_sturluson_by_br33zr-d5jea30.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1238620#post1238620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I may have misread or misunderstood something, but my impression of the Vice/Virtue flip is simply the way it earns WP, in other words it's easier to get all your WP back by indulging in the easy thing that's your Vice than it is to get any WP back from engaging your Virtue. Which makes sense to me considering the tortured state of ghosts, and the fact that they're trying to cling to their identity more than they're concerned with growing toward being a better person like the living are supposed to be doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Virtue is normally the harder one to recover, and Vice the easier one. For ghosts, that's reversed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-27T15:19:44-07:00","id":1239452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1235817-a-fright-of-ghosts-2e?p=1239437#post1239437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://pre00.deviantart.net/1480/th/pre/i/2012/302/2/3/celty_sturluson_by_br33zr-d5jea30.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Virtue is normally the harder one to recover, and Vice the easier one. For ghosts, that's reversed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, thank you for restating the obvious and not actually engaging with what I was saying about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-28T12:52:18-07:00","id":1239768,"title":"","content":"More Ghosts! <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Blackheart Jean-Philippe</b></span><br /> \u201cBlackheart\u201d Jean-Philippe is the ghost of a notorious pirate that lived during what is considered the Golden Age of Piracy. Once a slave, Jean-Philippe took to piracy and raided the waters surrounding Haiti in the early 1700\u2019s before being slain in battle. Even as a ghost, Jean-Philippe retains a sense of adventure and taste for the pleasures of wine, song, and sensuality. He is pragmatically ruthless, and thinks little of permanently dispatching enemies.<br /> Jean-Philippe appears by turn either a handsome Haitian man with an athletic build, or a moldering skeletal corpse. He is anchored to his cutlass blade, which remains in excellent condition, with a bright polish and fresh leather wrapping on its hilt. The blade has moved through various museum collections, but was stolen 10 years ago. It\u2019s current whereabouts are unknown.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Ghost]<br /> <b>Power</b> 4 <b>Finesse</b> 6 <b>Resistance</b> 4, <b>Willpower</b> 10, <b>Essence</b> 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 15<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Adventurous, <b>Vice</b> Ruthless<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To seek adventure and fortune<br /> <b>Key Skills:</b> Streetwise, Weaponry<br /> <b>Key Merits:</b> Professional Training (Pirate)<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Anchor (Cutlass) 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must honor a declaration of truce; <b>Bane:</b> rum mixed with sea water<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Fetter, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Blast (Pistol), Firestarter, Pathfinder, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Cassandra Silver</span></b><br /> Cassandra Silver (given name Anne Griswold) was a talented up and coming actress cast the femme fatale in a noir detective film titled Midnight Heart in 1946. During the final week of filming, Cassandra was found dead in her Malibu home. Despite evidence of violence and sexual assault, the city coroner ruled her death \u201csuicide\u201d and the case closed with little fanfare.<br /> Midnight Heart was never released, despite the director\u2019s efforts to edit the film to account for the un-shot scenes.<br /> During the filming the production of an earlier film, Cassandra began an affair with the director which continued on into the production of Midnight Heart. All of this was kept hidden by the studio, as the director was a married man and the scandal would have been disastrous. When she broke off the affair the director flew into a rage and murdered her. The situation was quickly covered up by Solomon Studios and a heavily bribed police force. As most of the people involved are long dead, it is unlikely the truth about Cassandra Silvers death will ever be known.<br /> Her ghost remains anchored to the last known copy of the film.<br /> Cassandra is still a stunning beauty, with blue eyes, porcelain skin, an hourglass figure and silver-blond hair. Although those she sought her revenge against are all dead, Cassandra lingers on.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Ghost]<br /> <b>Power</b> 5 <b>Finesse</b> 5, <b>Resistance</b> 4, <b>Willpower</b> 9, <b>Essence</b> 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 15<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Ambitious, <b>Vice</b> Bitter<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Recapture her fame<br /> <b>Key Skills:</b> Expression, Socialize<br /> <b>Key Merits:</b> Striking Looks 2<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Anchor (Midnight Heart) 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest where a non-digital filming device is running <b>Bane:</b> Silver<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Fetter, Image, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast (Telekinetic Thrust), Hallucination, Rapture, Sign, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sexton Darwin</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sexton Darwin was the lead vocalist of a 5 member black metal band named \u201cWound\u201d, and was known for a hard-partying lifestyle and dabbling in the occult. The entire band was found dead in late 1990 in what appeared to be a ritualistic murder/suicide. His ghost remains anchored to an unlabeled black cassette that contains the only known copy of Wound's final album.<br /> Sexton still looks the part of a late 80\u2019s rocker in the black metal scene; black leather pants, black t-shirt, long dark hair and arms covered in satanic and occult tattoos and fists adorned with menacing silver jewelry. Death has made his pale flesh almost white and turned his eyes into smoldering red pinpoints.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Ghost]<br /> <b>Power</b> 6 <b>Finesse</b> 4, <b>Resistance</b> 4, <b>Willpower</b> 8, <b>Essence</b> 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 8, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 15<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Artistic, <b>Vice</b> Hatred<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Promote Nihilism and Self Destructive behavior<br /> <b>Key Skills:</b> Expression, Occult<br /> <b>Key Merits:</b> Inspiring<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Anchor (Black Cassette) 2, Nihilism 1<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot harm a person wearing a \u201cWound\u201d t-shirt or patch. <b>Bane:</b> Consecrated Salt<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Fetter, Unfetter, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast (Death Metal Scream), Dement, Implant Mission, Sign</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-30T00:31:11-07:00","id":1240345,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Still On Patrol</b></u> <div align=\"left\">In 1963, the US nuclear submarine <i>Blackjack </i>left port to conduct diving tests off the coast of Massachusetts. It has just come off a longer-than-expected retrofit, and the Navy was eager to get it through a shakedown and back into service. The <i>Blackjack </i>commenced a dive test at 8 o\u2019clock in the morning on April 9; its last, garbled communication was heard two hours later, followed shortly by the distinctive sound of an implosion. After two days of fruitless searching, the <i>Blackjack </i>was declared lost with all hands.<br /> </div> <div align=\"left\">A subsequent investigation came to no definite conclusions about the ship\u2019s loss. Engineers floated theories about ruptured pipes and reactor meltdowns, while a few intelligence operatives whispered about top-secret Soviet weapons projects. A deep-sea submersible deployed in the 80s finally located the debris field; radioactivity levels were too high, and the individual pieces too small, for any sort of recovery to be feasible.<br /> </div> <div align=\"left\">The <i>Blackjack </i>now exists as perhaps the largest and most inaccessible Castoff in the world. The ghost ship circles the debris field over eight thousand feet below the surface, unable to move away. Other ships, particularly military vessels, sometimes receive staticky, distorted radio transmissions when near the <i>Blackjack\u2019s </i>wreckage, or see the ship surface briefly in the distance.<br /> </div> <div align=\"left\">If someone were to successfully board the ship, they would find it empty except for a few Rank 1 ghosts of the crew, re-enacting the fatal dive test in perpetuity. The submarine itself, however, has a certain basic intelligence; it tries to draw in the living, in hopes that the truth of its destruction will become known, and it can finally finish its mission<br /> .</div> <div align=\"left\"><b>The USS Blackjack</b></div> <div align=\"left\"><b>Rank: </b>2<br /> <b>Durability: </b>5<br /> <b>Structure: </b>55<br /> <b>Speed: </b>30<br /> <b>Size: </b>50<br /> <b>Attributes:</b></div> <div align=\"left\"><i>Power 5 Finesse 2 Resistance 7</i></div> <div align=\"left\"><b>Essence</b>: 15<br /> <b>Numina:</b>Implant Mission, Emotional Aura, Sign, Hallucination<br /> <b>Bane: </b>Enriched uranium<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Must attempt to surface at the sound of a bell (will put the sub outside the Anchor condition)<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Anchor (wreckage) 1, Sea 2<br /> <b>Manifestations: </b>Twilight Form, Image, Materialize</div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <b>Blackjack Crew Member </b></div> <div align=\"left\">Rank: 1<br /> <b>Size: </b>5<br /> <b>Corpus: </b>8<br /> <b>Willpower: </b>6<br /> <b>Initiative: </b>6<br /> <b>Defense: </b>3<br /> <b>Speed: </b>11<br /> <b>Attributes:</b></div> <div align=\"left\"><i>Power 3 Finesse 3 Resistance 3</i></div> <div align=\"left\"><b>Essence</b>: 10<br /> <b>Numina:</b>Blast (radiation)<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>7<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Anchor (wreckage) 1<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Must stop to return a salute<br /> <b>Bane: </b>Salt water<br /> <b>Manifestations: </b>Twilight Form, Image<br /> <br /> <b>Plot Hooks </b><br /> <br /> *Someone who saw the Blackjack surface or heard one of its phantom transmissions is now obsessed with uncovering the truth behind its sinking. They ask the krewe for help gathering information.<br /> <br /> *Owing to environmental concerns, the Navy has decided to raise the Blackjack's nuclear reactor in order to seal it off and move it to a more secure storage facility. The Blackjack and its ghostly crew now have two Anchors - the reactor, and the rest of the debris field. Will this help them communicate with the living? What happens when a 278-foot submarine Materializes on dry land?<br /> <br /> *The krewe has an idea for how to explore the Rivers of the Underworld (or possibly the Ocean of Fragments itself). They just have to get aboard the Castoff sub, and figure out how to get it into the Underworld. Oh, and how to steer....</div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","user":"Mad_Maudlin","date":". 07-30-2018, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}